a field is an option, which takes the next argument or what follows = after --name
a required field of each kind, an optional list and a set
positional fields take the arguments in order, and the field after_dashes those after --
arguments that do not fit throw an ArgsError that names the option or the argument
a value that is no value of the field type throws an ArgsError
a Float takes inf
the usage message shows the positional arguments, then the options with their defaults
a required list of an enum takes its members
parse_command takes the command that the first argument names, with - for _
a spec that does not fit the struct throws a ValueError
options that two fields would share, or positional arguments out of order, throw
a struct that std:args cannot read arguments into throws a ValueError
